    "https://yorkvilleuniversity.applytojob.com/apply/jobs/details/RbfmscZdOW?&": {
      "title": "Associate Admissions Advisor",
      "description": "JazzHR » Job Listings « Back to Jobs Yorkville University Associate Admissions Advisor Admissions - Remote - Full Time Who we are At Yorkville University and Toronto Film School, we believe education is more than the pursuit of knowledge – it is a catalyst for transformation. Our mission, grounded in democratizing education, is to create access for learners from every background and empower them to achieve their aspirations and advance their careers. We are committed to delivering rigorous, flexible programs that are both personally fulfilling and professionally rewarding, while contributing to the betterment of society. Since 2004, Yorkville has been among Canada’s few private, for-profit, fully accredited degree-granting universities, with campuses in Ontario, British Columbia, and New Brunswick. Together with Toronto Film School, we offer creative and academic pathways at both the college and university levels, cultivating a multidisciplinary environment where innovation and the arts converge. Our community is vibrant and diverse. Many of our learners are adults balancing education with careers and personal commitments. Every member of our team – whether in teaching, operations, or technology – is dedicated to removing barriers and expanding access. Together, we deliver flexible, industry-informed learning that leads to meaningful opportunities. At our core is human connection – guiding people to reimagine their futures in a community defined by opportunity, creativity, and growth. Who we need Reporting to the Associate Director of Admissions, we are hiring an Associate Admissions Advisor to support prospective students exploring programs at Yorkville University and Toronto Film School. As our new Associate Admissions Advisor, you will be one of the first points of connection for prospective students, reaching out to understand their educational and career goals, explore their motivation for returning to school, and determine whether their program of interest aligns with what they want to achieve. You will build rapport through high-volume outbound calls, answer initial questions, qualify prospective students, and connect engaged candidates with an Admissions Advisor who can guide them through the next steps in their journey. This is a fully remote role for candidates based in Ontario. The schedule is 1:00–9:00 p.m. ET, with a bi-weekly Saturday shift. What's in it for you A clear path for career growth. This role is designed as a stepping stone to becoming an Admissions Advisor. You will build the communication, relationship-building, and sales skills needed to take the next step in your career while gaining hands-on experience connecting with prospective students, understanding their goals, and guiding them toward the right next step. A chance to build your sales skills. Whether you are bringing customer service experience or are earlier in your sales career, you will have the opportunity to strengthen your ability to build rapport, ask thoughtful questions, listen for what matters, and confidently engage people over the phone. You will work toward clear goals and KPIs, with the opportunity to earn commission based on your performance. Support to learn and succeed. You will join leaders who value open communication, coaching, and development. You will have the opportunity to learn from experienced Admissions professionals, receive feedback on your approach, and build the confidence and skills to take on greater responsibility as you grow. As our new Associate Admissions Advisor, you will Connect with prospective students. You will conduct high-volume outbound outreach to people who have expressed interest in Yorkville University or Toronto Film School. You will create a positive first impression, build rapport quickly, answer initial questions, and engage prospective students in meaningful conversations about their education and career goals. Understand their goals and motivation. You will ask thoughtful questions and actively listen to understand what is motivating each prospective student to explore further education. You will help them consider whether their program of interest aligns with their goals and identify those who are ready to continue the conversation with an Admissions Advisor. Create a seamless next step. You will pre-qualify prospective students and connect engaged, qualified individuals with an Admissions Advisor through scheduled appointments or live transfers. You will help maintain a strong pipeline by keeping conversations moving forward and working toward established outreach and conversion goals. Manage your outreach and results. You will take ownership of a high-volume calling schedule, accurately track your activity, and work toward individual and team KPIs. You will use the team's systems and processes to stay organized, manage follow-ups, and ensure prospective student information is captured accurately. Contribute to the Admissions team. You will work closely with Admissions Advisors and your fellow Associate Admissions Advisors to support prospective students and team goals. You will share insights, participate in team activities and recruiting initiatives, and contribute to an inclusive, collaborative environment focused on student success. What you bring The communication skills. You are a confident and engaging communicator who can quickly build rapport over the phone. You ask thoughtful questions, listen closely, and adapt your approach based on what you hear, helping prospective students feel comfortable sharing their goals, motivations, and concerns. The customer-focused approach. You have experience working directly with customers, clients, or the public in a service, sales, retail, call centre, or similarly people-focused environment. You know how to create a positive experience while guiding a conversation toward a clear next step. The drive and resilience. You are motivated by goals and comfortable working toward measurable targets. You can maintain your energy through a high volume of outreach, stay positive when a conversation does not go as planned, and move confidently to the next opportunity. The self-management skills. You can structure your day, manage follow-ups, and stay focused in a remote environment. You are organized and accountable, with the ability to balance a consistent outreach schedule with accurate documentation and attention to detail. The motivation to learn. You are open to feedback, coaching, and new approaches that will help you strengthen your sales and relationship-building skills. You are curious, eager to develop, and ready to take ownership of your performance while contributing to the success of the broader Admissions team. Why work at Yorkville University? At Yorkville University and Toronto Film School, we are united by a shared purpose: placing the student experience at the heart of everything we do. Whether you are teaching, designing curriculum, advising students, advancing technology, or supporting operations, your work directly fuels learning potential, strengthens inclusive communities, and fosters purposeful curiosity. Here, professional growth is part of our culture. In your role, you will have opportunities to help the launch of career-relevant programs, expand your expertise, and access tuition-free courses across our institutions - from certificates to master’s degrees. Curiosity, initiative, and innovation are encouraged, and your ideas can move from vision to reality. Our scale offers the best of both worlds: the reach and stability of a national institution combined with the agility of a mid-sized organization, where contributions are visible and valued. You will be part of a diverse and inclusive community where authenticity is celebrated, collaboration is expected, and impact is shared - on students, colleagues, and your own professional journey. At Yorkville and Toronto Film School, your work does more than make a difference. It empowers others to achieve their possible, while giving you the opportunity to realize yours. Compensation philosophy At Yorkville University and Toronto Film School, we believe compensation should be fair, straightforward, and supportive of your growth. Our salary ranges reflect progression from learning in the role to excelling, with each offer based on skills, experience, and role complexity. This role offers a fixed annual base salary of $45,000 plus competitive commission. We strive for equitable, consistent pay, though rates may vary within the same role based on performance, specialized knowledge, and impact. Base salary is one part of a broader package that includes paid time away, retirement savings matching, and extended health coverage with 80% of premiums paid. After 12 months of full-time employment, there is also tuition-free access to all our education programs. We welcome conversations about compensation throughout the hiring process. Join us We welcome and appreciate candidates with a range of backgrounds and experiences. If you have 70% of the qualifications we seek, express your interest. What you can expect from our hiring process: A virtual interview with a Talent Advisor to discuss your interest in joining the company and in the role. The conversation will be recorded using BrightHire, an AI-powered video interview tool. More details will be shared when you are invited to interview. A virtual interview with the Associate Director of Admissions and a member of the team. You will have the opportunity to share more about your experience, communication style, and approach to building relationships and achieving goals. A final virtual interview with the Associate Directors of Admissions for Yorkville University and Toronto Film School and the Director. You will have an opportunity to meet members of the leadership team and learn more about the role and the Admissions team. Diversity, equity, and inclusion are critical components of life at Yorkville University and Toronto Film School, and we are committed to making these values an integral part of our culture. We encourage applications from all qualified applicants, including women, persons with disabilities, Black, Indigenous and People of Colour (BIPOC), people from the Lesbian, Gay, Bisexual, Transgender, Transsexual, Queer, Questioning, Two-Spirit, Intersex, Asexual + (LGBTQ2SIA+) community and other equity-seeking groups. Yorkville University is committed to providing accessible employment practices that comply with the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). If you require accommodation for disability, please notify Human Resources at 1-877-429-4029. #LI-DNI #LI-Remote Apply Now Share Job Apply: Associate Admissions Advisor * Required fields First name* Last name* Email address* Location Phone number* Resume* Attach resume or Paste resume Attach resume as .pdf, .doc, .docx, .odt, .txt, or .rtf (limit 5MB) or paste resume Paste your resume here or attach resume file Help us maintain an inclusive culture. We want anyone, anywhere to have the same chance and opportunity to build a life they love and that they are proud of. We are proactive in creating a belonging environment that anyone can be a part of. Thoughtful, data-driven decision-making is core to this success. We ask these questions to strengthen our practices by using data to identify and mitigate unconscious bias in our hiring process. If you choose to answer them, the responses are ONLY used in aggregate to help us identify areas for improvement in our processes. Your responses, or your choice to prefer not to say, will not be associated with your application and will not in any way be used in the hiring decision. For one, that’s illegal, and we’re really not into breaking the law. Keep being awesome, and thank you for considering work at Yorkville University. 1) Indigenous peoples: Based on the definition below, are you an Indigenous person? \"Indigenous peoples\" means First Nations, Inuit or Métis peoples of Canada.* -- No answer -- Yes No I prefer not to say 2) Persons with disabilities: Based on the definition below, are you a person with a disability? \"Persons with disabilities\" are individuals who have a long-term or recurring physical, mental, sensory, psychiatric, or learning impairment, and who consider themselves to be disadvantaged in employment by reason of that impairment, or believe that an employer or potential employer is likely to consider them to be disadvantaged in employment by reason of that impairment. This includes persons whose functional limitations owing to their impairment have been accommodated in their current job or workplace.* -- No answer -- No Yes, visible disability Yes, non-visible disability (e.g., learning disability, mental health condition, hearing/visual impairments) Yes, both visible and non-visible disability Unsure/Do not know Prefer not to answer 3) Members of visible minorities: Based on the definition below, are you a member of a visible minority? \"Members of visible minorities\" are persons, other than Indigenous peoples, who are non-Caucasian in race or non-white in colour, regardless of birthplace.* -- No answer -- Yes No I prefer not to say 4) To which gender do you most identify?* -- No answer -- Male (Cisgender) Female (Cisgender) Transgender Female Transgender Male Gender Variant/Non-Conforming Non-Binary Genderfluid Intersex Not Listed I prefer not to say 5) What are your salary expectations?* 6) Are you legally eligible to work in Canada on an ongoing basis?* -- No answer -- Yes No 7) Preferred Name 8) Have you previously worked for Yorkville University or Toronto Film School, or are you currently employed here?* -- No answer -- Yes No 9) If you have been referred by a Yorkville University or Toronto Film School employee, include their first and last name below. If this is not applicable, type 'N/A' below.* Human Check *"
