    "https://yorkvilleuniversity.applytojob.com/apply/jobs/details/qQ02SkWKkl?&": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant",
      "description": "JazzHR » Job Listings « Back to Jobs Yorkville University Executive Assistant Principal & VP Academic - New Westminster, BC, Canada - Full Time Who we are At Yorkville University and Toronto Film School, we believe education is more than the pursuit of knowledge – it is a catalyst for transformation. Our mission, grounded in democratizing education, is to create access for learners from every background and empower them to achieve their aspirations and advance their careers. We are committed to delivering rigorous, flexible programs that are both personally fulfilling and professionally rewarding, while contributing to the betterment of society. Since 2004, Yorkville has been among Canada’s few private, for-profit, fully accredited degree-granting universities, with campuses in Ontario, British Columbia, and New Brunswick. Together with Toronto Film School, we offer creative and academic pathways at both the college and university levels, cultivating a multidisciplinary environment where innovation and the arts converge. Our community is vibrant and diverse. Many of our learners are adults balancing education with careers and personal commitments. Every member of our team – whether in teaching, operations, or technology – is dedicated to removing barriers and expanding access. Together, we deliver flexible, industry-informed learning that leads to meaningful opportunities. At our core is human connection – guiding people to reimagine their futures in a community defined by opportunity, creativity, and growth. Who we need Reporting to and supporting the Principal & VP Academic, we are hiring an Executive Assistant to provide high-level executive support in a highly visible role. As our new Executive Assistant, you will act as a trusted partner, managing priorities, coordinating communications, and ensuring the smooth operation of a busy executive office. Working across leadership teams, you will coordinate meetings, support governance activities and strategic initiatives, and serve as a central point of contact while exercising sound judgment, discretion, and professionalism in every interaction. This is a full time on-site role based in New Westminster, BC. What’s in it for you? This is an opportunity to play a key role in supporting the leadership team on a dynamic and collaborative campus. As the Executive Assistant, you will partner closely with the Vice President Academic, Dean, and Associate Chairs, helping bring structure to competing priorities, coordinating key initiatives, and ensuring the smooth day-to-day operation of the academic leadership office. Working across the campus community, you will build strong relationships with faculty, staff, and students, provide high-level administrative support, and contribute to processes that enhance the effectiveness of academic programs and campus operations. As our new Executive Assistant, you will: Create clarity. You will bring structure to competing priorities, ensuring your executive is prepared, informed, and focused on what matters most. Through thoughtful planning, sound judgment, and a proactive approach, you will anticipate needs, manage changing demands, and keep work moving forward with confidence. Drive execution. You will oversee a complex and ever-changing schedule, coordinate meetings and events, prepare correspondence, presentations, and briefing materials, and manage follow-up actions. You will be the person who connects the details, ensuring commitments are met and nothing falls through the cracks. Build trusted relationships. Working across the organization, you will partner with senior leaders and key stakeholders, acting as a central point of coordination for executive activities and strategic initiatives. Your professionalism, discretion, and ability to navigate competing priorities will make you a trusted resource and valued partner. Strengthen how the executive office operates. In a growing, evolving organization, you will continuously look for opportunities to improve processes, introduce efficiencies, and enhance the way work gets done. Whether refining workflows, implementing new approaches, or identifying opportunities for improvement, you will help build an executive office that is proactive, responsive, and positioned to support a scaling business. You bring: The foresight. You know how to stay three steps ahead. You anticipate needs before they arise, adapt quickly as priorities shift, and use sound judgment to make informed decisions in a dynamic environment. You are at your best when bringing calm, structure, and momentum to complex work. The organizational expertise. You have experience supporting senior leaders while managing multiple priorities with accuracy and professionalism. From coordinating complex calendars and executive meetings to preparing polished materials and tracking critical follow-up actions, you create confidence through your attention to detail and exceptional execution. The relationship-building skills. You communicate with professionalism, tact, and discretion, building trust with leaders, colleagues, and stakeholders at every level. You know how to navigate sensitive situations, handle confidential information, and collaborate effectively across teams. The drive to improve. You don't simply maintain processes—you look for ways to make them better. Resourceful and proactive, you enjoy solving problems, identifying efficiencies, and finding practical solutions that help people work more effectively. You take pride in being someone others can depend on to deliver high-quality work and keep important priorities moving. Why work at Yorkville University? At Yorkville University and Toronto Film School, we are united by a shared purpose: placing the student experience at the heart of everything we do. Whether you are teaching, designing curriculum, advising students, advancing technology, or supporting operations, your work directly fuels learning potential, strengthens inclusive communities, and fosters purposeful curiosity. Here, professional growth is part of our culture. In your role, you will have opportunities to help the launch of career-relevant programs, expand your expertise, and access tuition-free courses across our institutions - from certificates to master’s degrees. Curiosity, initiative, and innovation are encouraged, and your ideas can move from vision to reality. Our scale offers the best of both worlds: the reach and stability of a national institution combined with the agility of a mid-sized organization, where contributions are visible and valued. You will be part of a diverse and inclusive community where authenticity is celebrated, collaboration is expected, and impact is shared - on students, colleagues, and your own professional journey. At Yorkville and Toronto Film School, your work does more than make a difference. It empowers others to achieve their possible, while giving you the opportunity to realize yours. Compensation philosophy At Yorkville University and Toronto Film School, we believe compensation should be fair, straightforward, and supportive of your growth. Our salary ranges reflect progression from learning in the role to excelling, with each offer based on skills, experience, and role complexity. This position offers a minimum annual salary of $75,000, a midpoint of $77,500 and a maximum of $80,000. Established hires typically start near the midpoint, while the upper range is reserved for those with deep expertise and sustained contributions. Offers below the midpoint recognize strong potential with room to grow. We strive for equitable, consistent pay, though rates may vary within the same role based on performance, specialized knowledge, and impact. We welcome conversations about compensation throughout the hiring process. Join us We welcome and appreciate candidates with a range of backgrounds and experiences. If you have 70% of the qualifications we seek, express your interest. What you can expect from the interview process: A virtual interview with a Talent Advisor to discuss your interest in the role and your experience. The conversation will be recorded using BrightHire, an AI-powered interview platform. More details will be shared when you are invited to interview. A virtual interview with the Human Resources team and the Hiring Manager focused on your experience supporting senior leaders, your approach to managing competing priorities, and how you build trusted relationships. A virtual interview with a member of the executive team to explore your communication style, judgment, problem-solving approach, and how you would contribute in a collaborative, fast-evolving organization. A final on-site interview. You will have the opportunity to get a campus tour, meet some of the team, and ask any final questions you may have about the role. Diversity, equity, and inclusion are critical components of life at Yorkville University and Toronto Film School, and we are committed to making these values an integral part of our culture. We encourage applications from all qualified applicants, including women, persons with disabilities, Black, Indigenous and People of Colour (BIPOC), people from the Lesbian, Gay, Bisexual, Transgender, Transsexual, Queer, Questioning, Two-Spirit, Intersex, Asexual + (LGBTQ2SIA+) community and other equity-seeking groups. Yorkville University is committed to providing accessible employment practices that comply with the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). If you require accommodation for disability, please notify Human Resources at 1-877-429-4029. #LI-DNI Apply Now Share Job Apply: Executive Assistant * Required fields First name* Last name* Email address* Location Phone number* Resume* Attach resume or Paste resume Attach resume as .pdf, .doc, .docx, .odt, .txt, or .rtf (limit 5MB) or paste resume Paste your resume here or attach resume file Help us maintain an inclusive culture. We want anyone, anywhere to have the same chance and opportunity to build a life they love and that they are proud of. We are proactive in creating a belonging environment that anyone can be a part of. Thoughtful, data-driven decision-making is core to this success. We ask these questions to strengthen our practices by using data to identify and mitigate unconscious bias in our hiring process. If you choose to answer them, the responses are ONLY used in aggregate to help us identify areas for improvement in our processes. Your responses, or your choice to prefer not to say, will not be associated with your application and will not in any way be used in the hiring decision. For one, that’s illegal, and we’re really not into breaking the law. Keep being awesome, and thank you for considering work at Yorkville University. 1) Indigenous peoples: Based on the definition below, are you an Indigenous person? \"Indigenous peoples\" means First Nations, Inuit or Métis peoples of Canada.* -- No answer -- Yes No I prefer not to say 2) Persons with disabilities: Based on the definition below, are you a person with a disability? \"Persons with disabilities\" are individuals who have a long-term or recurring physical, mental, sensory, psychiatric, or learning impairment, and who consider themselves to be disadvantaged in employment by reason of that impairment, or believe that an employer or potential employer is likely to consider them to be disadvantaged in employment by reason of that impairment. This includes persons whose functional limitations owing to their impairment have been accommodated in their current job or workplace.* -- No answer -- No Yes, visible disability Yes, non-visible disability (e.g., learning disability, mental health condition, hearing/visual impairments) Yes, both visible and non-visible disability Unsure/Do not know Prefer not to answer 3) Members of visible minorities: Based on the definition below, are you a member of a visible minority? \"Members of visible minorities\" are persons, other than Indigenous peoples, who are non-Caucasian in race or non-white in colour, regardless of birthplace.* -- No answer -- Yes No I prefer not to say 4) To which gender do you most identify?* -- No answer -- Male (Cisgender) Female (Cisgender) Transgender Female Transgender Male Gender Variant/Non-Conforming Non-Binary Genderfluid Intersex Not Listed I prefer not to say 5) What are your salary expectations?* 6) Are you legally eligible to work in Canada on an ongoing basis?* -- No answer -- Yes No 7) Preferred Name 8) Have you previously worked for Yorkville University or Toronto Film School, or are you currently employed here?* -- No answer -- Yes No 9) If you have been referred by a Yorkville University or Toronto Film School employee, include their first and last name below. If this is not applicable, type 'N/A' below.* 10) This is a full-time, on-site position based in New Westminster, BC. Are you currently located in the Greater Vancouver area or able to reliably commute to the campus?* -- No answer -- Yes No 11) Do you have at least 2 years experience providing executive-level support to senior leaders, including managing complex calendars, meetings, and priorities?* -- No answer -- Yes No 12) Are you comfortable working fully on-site in a role supporting senior academic leadership and interacting with stakeholders across campus?* -- No answer -- Yes No 13) Do you have experience providing administrative support to senior leaders (e.g., executives, VPs, Deans, Directors, or equivalent)?* -- No answer -- Yes No 14) Do you have experience managing complex calendars, coordinating meetings, preparing executive materials, and handling confidential information?* -- No answer -- Yes No Human Check *"
    },
    "https://yorkvilleuniversity.applytojob.com/apply/jobs/details/5q8UqR75Jk?&": {
      "title": "Office Manager",
      "description": "JazzHR » Job Listings « Back to Jobs Yorkville University Office Manager Principal & VPA BC Campus - New Westminster, BC, Canada - Full Time Who we are At Yorkville University and Toronto Film School, we believe education is more than the pursuit of knowledge – it is a catalyst for transformation. Our mission, grounded in democratizing education, is to create access for learners from every background and empower them to achieve their aspirations and advance their careers. We are committed to delivering rigorous, flexible programs that are both personally fulfilling and professionally rewarding, while contributing to the betterment of society. Since 2004, Yorkville has been among Canada’s few private, for-profit, fully accredited degree-granting universities, with campuses in Ontario, British Columbia, and New Brunswick. Together with Toronto Film School, we offer creative and academic pathways at both the college and university levels, cultivating a multidisciplinary environment where innovation and the arts converge. Our community is vibrant and diverse. Many of our learners are adults balancing education with careers and personal commitments. Every member of our team – whether in teaching, operations, or technology – is dedicated to removing barriers and expanding access. Together, we deliver flexible, industry-informed learning that leads to meaningful opportunities. At our core is human connection – guiding people to reimagine their futures in a community defined by opportunity, creativity, and growth. Who we need Reporting to the Principal & VPA BC Campus, we are hiring an Office Manager.  As our new Office Manager, you will be the visible, on-site leader responsible for creating a welcoming, well-run environment where employees, visitors, and partners can thrive. You will bring together office operations, facilities coordination, events, and community engagement under one cohesive function, ensuring the site runs smoothly while fostering collaboration across the organization. This is a full time on-site role based in New Westminster, BC. What’s in it for you Purpose beyond the workplace. Every role at Yorkville University contributes to creating an exceptional learning experience. While your focus will be on leading campus operations, your work will directly support the students, faculty, and staff who rely on a safe, welcoming, and well-run environment to learn, teach, and thrive. You will play an important role in helping deliver on our mission of expanding access to education and empowering learners to achieve their goals. A culture built on collaboration and growth. You will join an organization that values purposeful curiosity, inclusive leadership, and continuous improvement. Working closely with leaders across the BC campus and the broader university, you will have the opportunity to build meaningful relationships, contribute ideas, and shape how the campus experience continues to evolve. Your contributions will be visible, valued, and encouraged. An opportunity to grow with us. As Yorkville University continues to expand, so do the opportunities for our people. You will deepen your leadership and operational expertise while gaining exposure to facilities, events, community engagement, and people leadership. You'll also have access to tuition-free courses across Yorkville University and Toronto Film School, supporting your professional development and lifelong learning. As our new Office Manager, you will: Lead office operations. You will oversee the day-to-day operations of a busy campus, ensuring the workplace is welcoming, organized, and running efficiently. Acting as the central point of coordination, you will bring together office operations, facilities, events, and administrative support, creating consistency across functions and ensuring issues are addressed proactively. Solve operational challenges. You will take ownership of facilities coordination by responding quickly to building issues, working with vendors, and managing repairs and maintenance activities. Whether coordinating external service providers or resolving minor issues yourself, you will focus on finding practical solutions that minimize disruption and keep operations moving. Lead and support your team. You will manage and develop a small front desk and administrative team, providing coaching, guidance, and clear direction while fostering a collaborative, service-focused culture. You will ensure the team is equipped to deliver an exceptional experience for employees, visitors, and partners every day. Coordinate events and workplace experiences. You will oversee the logistics for meetings, special events, and larger organizational initiatives, working with internal stakeholders and external partners to ensure every detail is thoughtfully planned and executed. Your work will help create engaging experiences that strengthen connection and contribute to a positive workplace culture. Build relationships and drive collaboration. You will work closely with leaders and teams across the organization while also maintaining relationships with local organizations and community partners. Through your approachable, solutions-oriented style, you will strengthen communication, encourage collaboration, and help create an environment where people feel supported and connected. You bring: The leadership. You have experience leading and developing administrative or operational teams, creating an environment where people feel supported, accountable, and empowered to do their best work. You lead by example, communicate openly, and foster collaboration across teams. The operational expertise. You have successfully managed the day-to-day operations of a busy office or workplace, balancing competing priorities while ensuring people, processes, and resources come together seamlessly. You are highly organized, detail-oriented, and comfortable coordinating multiple responsibilities at once. The problem-solving mindset. You approach challenges with curiosity, resourcefulness, and a solutions-first attitude. Whether coordinating vendors, resolving facilities issues, or improving operational processes, you are comfortable taking ownership, making informed decisions, and following through to resolution. The relationship-building skills. You build trust quickly and communicate effectively with people at all levels of an organization and with external partners. You are approachable, collaborative, and enjoy creating positive experiences through thoughtful service and proactive communication. The adaptability. You enjoy variety and are comfortable shifting between strategic planning and hands-on execution. You are equally confident leading a team, organizing an event, coordinating operational priorities, or stepping in to help wherever needed to keep things running smoothly. Why work at Yorkville University? At Yorkville University and Toronto Film School, we are united by a shared purpose: placing the student experience at the heart of everything we do. Whether you are teaching, designing curriculum, advising students, advancing technology, or supporting operations, your work directly fuels learning potential, strengthens inclusive communities, and fosters purposeful curiosity. Here, professional growth is part of our culture. In your role, you will have opportunities to help the launch of career-relevant programs, expand your expertise, and access tuition-free courses across our institutions - from certificates to master’s degrees. Curiosity, initiative, and innovation are encouraged, and your ideas can move from vision to reality. Our scale offers the best of both worlds: the reach and stability of a national institution combined with the agility of a mid-sized organization, where contributions are visible and valued. You will be part of a diverse and inclusive community where authenticity is celebrated, collaboration is expected, and impact is shared - on students, colleagues, and your own professional journey. At Yorkville and Toronto Film School, your work does more than make a difference. It empowers others to achieve their possible, while giving you the opportunity to realize yours. Compensation philosophy At Yorkville University and Toronto Film School, we believe compensation should be fair, straightforward, and supportive of your growth. Our salary ranges reflect progression from learning in the role to excelling, with each offer based on skills, experience, and role complexity. This position offers a minimum annual salary of $75,000, a midpoint of $77,500 and a maximum of $80,000. Established hires typically start near the midpoint, while the upper range is reserved for those with deep expertise and sustained contributions. Offers below the midpoint recognize strong potential with room to grow. We strive for equitable, consistent pay, though rates may vary within the same role based on performance, specialized knowledge, and impact. We welcome conversations about compensation throughout the hiring process. Join us We welcome and appreciate candidates with a range of backgrounds and experiences. If you have 70% of the qualifications we seek, express your interest. What you can expect from the interview process: A virtual interview with a Talent Advisor to discuss your interest in the role and your experience. The conversation will be recorded using BrightHire, an AI-powered interview platform. More details will be shared when you are invited to interview. A virtual interview with HR and a member of the senior leadership team focused on your leadership experience, operational approach, and problem-solving style. A virtual interview with a member of the executive team to explore your communication style, judgment, problem-solving approach, and how you would contribute in a collaborative, fast-evolving organization. A final on-site interview. You will have the opportunity to get a campus tour, meet some of the team, and ask any final questions you may have about the role. Diversity, equity, and inclusion are critical components of life at Yorkville University and Toronto Film School, and we are committed to making these values an integral part of our culture. We encourage applications from all qualified applicants, including women, persons with disabilities, Black, Indigenous and People of Colour (BIPOC), people from the Lesbian, Gay, Bisexual, Transgender, Transsexual, Queer, Questioning, Two-Spirit, Intersex, Asexual + (LGBTQ2SIA+) community and other equity-seeking groups. Yorkville University is committed to providing accessible employment practices that comply with the Accessibility for Ontarians with Disabilities Act (AODA). If you require accommodation for disability, please notify Human Resources at 1-877-429-4029. #LI-DNI Apply Now Share Job Apply: Office Manager * Required fields First name* Last name* Email address* Location Phone number* Resume* Attach resume or Paste resume Attach resume as .pdf, .doc, .docx, .odt, .txt, or .rtf (limit 5MB) or paste resume Paste your resume here or attach resume file Help us maintain an inclusive culture. We want anyone, anywhere to have the same chance and opportunity to build a life they love and that they are proud of. We are proactive in creating a belonging environment that anyone can be a part of. Thoughtful, data-driven decision-making is core to this success. We ask these questions to strengthen our practices by using data to identify and mitigate unconscious bias in our hiring process. If you choose to answer them, the responses are ONLY used in aggregate to help us identify areas for improvement in our processes. Your responses, or your choice to prefer not to say, will not be associated with your application and will not in any way be used in the hiring decision. For one, that’s illegal, and we’re really not into breaking the law. Keep being awesome, and thank you for considering work at Yorkville University. 1) Indigenous peoples: Based on the definition below, are you an Indigenous person? \"Indigenous peoples\" means First Nations, Inuit or Métis peoples of Canada.* -- No answer -- Yes No I prefer not to say 2) Persons with disabilities: Based on the definition below, are you a person with a disability? \"Persons with disabilities\" are individuals who have a long-term or recurring physical, mental, sensory, psychiatric, or learning impairment, and who consider themselves to be disadvantaged in employment by reason of that impairment, or believe that an employer or potential employer is likely to consider them to be disadvantaged in employment by reason of that impairment. This includes persons whose functional limitations owing to their impairment have been accommodated in their current job or workplace.* -- No answer -- No Yes, visible disability Yes, non-visible disability (e.g., learning disability, mental health condition, hearing/visual impairments) Yes, both visible and non-visible disability Unsure/Do not know Prefer not to answer 3) Members of visible minorities: Based on the definition below, are you a member of a visible minority? \"Members of visible minorities\" are persons, other than Indigenous peoples, who are non-Caucasian in race or non-white in colour, regardless of birthplace.* -- No answer -- Yes No I prefer not to say 4) To which gender do you most identify?* -- No answer -- Male (Cisgender) Female (Cisgender) Transgender Female Transgender Male Gender Variant/Non-Conforming Non-Binary Genderfluid Intersex Not Listed I prefer not to say 5) What are your salary expectations?* 6) Are you legally eligible to work in Canada on an ongoing basis?* -- No answer -- Yes No 7) Preferred Name 8) Have you previously worked for Yorkville University or Toronto Film School, or are you currently employed here?* -- No answer -- Yes No 9) If you have been referred by a Yorkville University or Toronto Film School employee, include their first and last name below. If this is not applicable,